{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VFQarMBpCE7NZPzj7FifY6","type":"tool_result","content":"407:- [ ] **11 Lean: the forest regime.**\n408-  - **Question.** G. Which of items 06, 07 and 10 is within a session in\n409-    Lean, and prove it.\n410-  - **Method.** In order of reach, stop at the first that fills the\n411-    session: (a) **F1's blow-up lemma**: in a new file\n412-    `lean/MOSPFormalization/ForestCover.lean`, imported by\n413-    `lean/MOSPFormalization.lean`: the incidence graph of a `MOSPInstance`\n414-    as a `SimpleGraph (C ⊕ P)`; from a `PathDecomposition` of it of width\n415-    `w`, a path decomposition of `mospGraph M` of width `≤ (w + 1) · ω − 1`\n416-    (bags: the customers of the bag plus the customers of its patterns);\n417-    then, with `TreeBound.lean`'s `tree_pathwidth_le_treeBound` (per\n418-    component via `pathwidth_induce_le_of_forall_connected`), the\n419-    statement `IsAcyclic (incidence M) → mospValue M ≤ ω · (tb (n + m) + 1)`.\n420-    Check the statement numerically first on every forest instance of item\n421-    03 (`learning/sandwich.py` pins Lean definitions to the corpus\n422-    implementations; extend it). (b) The BFS layer lemma of item 07 (a),\n423-    deterministic: `vertexSeparation G ≤ max_i (|L_i| + |L_{i+1}|) − 1` for\n424-    the layer layout. (c) The coupling inclusion of item 10 (b) as a\n425-    statement about finsets: `A ⊆ A' → IsEmptyPair (coverGraph A') X Y →\n426-    IsEmptyPair (coverGraph A) X Y`, which is a two-line monotonicity\n427-    lemma over `CliqueCoverMoment.lean`'s definitions — do this one first\n428-    if (a) looks like more than a session, since it is cheap and the paper\n429-    can cite it.\n430-  - **Rules.** No `sorry`, no `axiom`; `lake build` passes; new theorems in\n431-    the new file only; `paper1/axiom_check.lean` extended; a stated gap is\n432-    acceptable only as a named `Prop` with the obstacle in PROGRESS.md.\n433-  - **Deliverable.** The Lean file; its names and axiom lines in\n434-    `reports/excess_phase_diagram.md` §11; `learning/sandwich.py`'s sorry\n435-    inventory still at zero.\n436-  - **Kill criterion.** None; \"blocked with the obstacle\" is a deliverable.\n437-  - **Size range.** Not applicable.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Regression gate for loop0010 (the excess phase diagram).\n\nPasses only if all five hold:\n1. `lake build` in lean/ succeeds;\n2. every `.lean` file under lean/MOSPFormalization/ (top level, Complex/ and\n   Search/) is imported by lean/MOSPFormalization.lean, so the build really\n   checks it;\n3. the number of `sorry` in Lean *code* (comments and docstrings stripped) is\n   at most the baseline (0: the development has none since Appendix E) plus\n   the entries in allowed_sorries.txt, and no `axiom` declaration exists;\n4. `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x` passes, and so does `pytest` in\n   pathwidth_solver/;\n5. the paper builds with no undefined references (`make -C paper1/latex check`).\n\n    python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0010/gate.py\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO = HERE.parents[1]\nLEAN = REPO / \"lean\"\nBASELINE_SORRIES = 0\nALLOWED = HERE / \"allowed_sorries.txt\"\nPAPER = REPO / \"paper1\" / \"latex\"\n\n\ndef strip_comments(src: str) -> str:\n    out, i, depth = [], 0, 0\n    while i < len(src):\n        if src.startswith(\"/-\", i):\n            depth += 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth and src.startswith(\"-/\", i):\n            depth -= 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth:\n            i += 1; continue\n        if src.startswith(\"--\", i):\n            j = src.find(\"\\n\", i); i = len(src) if j < 0 else j; continue\n        if src[i] == '\"':\n            j = i + 1\n            while j < len(src) and src[j] != '\"':\n                j += 2 if src[j] == \"\\\\\" else 1\n            i = j + 1; continue\n      